From d708861bda280ef95cf23b7e5d7bc878cb202877 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 20:03:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 302/303] player.c -- the next icon during a stream asks the
 station list

The press handlers have branched on s_streaming since 0206: next and
previous go to stations_next()/stations_prev() while a stream is running
rather than to the playlist. The icon never learned, so it is still lit
or greyed by playlist_has_next(), which answers a question about files in
a folder at a moment when there is no folder.

Both answers it can give are wrong. Lit with a one-station list, so the
button invites a press whose entire effect is to log "no other station in
the list" -- and CLAUDE.md records that next and previous have never been
tested on hardware, because no flash so far has had a stations.m3u with
two entries in it, so this has been the state every run was in. Greyed
with a full station list, if the folder behind the stream happened to be
at its last track, which hides a button that works.

stations_have_other() rather than count > 1: it is the same call the
press handlers and streamplan_transport() make, and one place deciding
the one-station case is what keeps the icon from drifting away from the
action it describes.

Asked every repaint, which the line above it already was and for the same
reason -- the station list can be reloaded underneath.

Previous gets no equivalent and needs none: the bar has never greyed it,
because on a file there is always something for it to do.
---
 main/player.c | 23 ++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/main/player.c b/main/player.c
index 2eef011..afaa992 100644
--- a/main/player.c
+++ b/main/player.c
@@ -5282,7 +5282,28 @@ static void ui_task(void *arg)
          * chooser can load a different folder underneath, and a next
          * button greyed against a playlist that no longer exists is
          * worse than one that is briefly right for the wrong reason. */
-        st.has_next = playlist_has_next(browser_order());
+        /*
+         * And during a stream it asks the station list instead, because
+         * that is what the button does then.
+         *
+         * UI_ACTION_NEXT and UI_ACTION_PREV have branched on s_streaming
+         * since 0206 -- a press goes to stations_next() rather than
+         * playlist_next() -- but nothing told the icon, so it went on
+         * being greyed or lit by playlist_has_next(), which answers about
+         * files in a folder and there is no folder here. Both answers it
+         * can give are wrong: lit with one station, so the button invites
+         * a press that logs "no other station in the list" and does
+         * nothing; greyed with a full station list if the folder behind
+         * the stream happened to be at its last track, which hides a
+         * button that works.
+         *
+         * stations_have_other() and not count > 1, so the one-station
+         * case is still decided in one place -- it is the same call the
+         * press handlers and streamplan_transport() make, which is what
+         * keeps the icon and the action from drifting apart.
+         */
+        st.has_next = s_streaming ? stations_have_other()
+                                  : playlist_has_next(browser_order());
 
         /*
          * The staged text becomes the shown text when the art has
